From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:38:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: register image textures for Metal validation

Apple's residency sets make a heap they hold resident together with
every resource placed in it, so the device set, which holds the heaps,
already keeps every image texture resident. Metal's API and shader
validation check each texture a command buffer reaches against the
sets by itself, though. API validation reports every attachment as "not
added to any residency set", and shader validation silently drops the
image loads and stores it does not find there: under
MTL_SHADER_VALIDATION=1, a vertex shader copying a cube map array image
read and wrote nothing, as KHR-GLES31.core.texture_cube_map_array
image_op_vertex_sh did through Zink.

While a validation layer wraps the Metal device, which the device's
class shows once at creation, the driver now registers the textures of
images when they are bound and the textures views make themselves, and
removes them on destruction. Registering costs about 1.4 us per image
view lifetime on an M1 Ultra, a third of creating and destroying one,
so a device without validation registers nothing. The texel buffer
textures, registered always until now for the same reason, follow the
same rule.

kosmickrisp_validated_image_access runs the cube map array copy under
MTL_SHADER_VALIDATION=1 and checks every texel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
